## Vercel Speed Insights Installation

Successfully installed and configured Vercel Speed Insights for this Next.js App Router project.

### Changes Made

#### 1. Package Installation
- Installed `@vercel/speed-insights` version 2.0.0 using npm
- Updated `package.json` with the new dependency
- Updated `package-lock.json` with resolved dependencies

#### 2. Component Integration
- Modified `src/app/layout.tsx` to integrate the SpeedInsights component:
  - Added import: `import { SpeedInsights } from "@vercel/speed-insights/next";`
  - Added the `<SpeedInsights />` component at the end of the `<body>` tag

### Implementation Details

Following the official Vercel documentation (fetched from https://vercel.com/docs/speed-insights/quickstart), I used the Next.js App Router-specific integration pattern which:
- Uses the `@vercel/speed-insights/next` import path (optimized for Next.js 13.5+)
- Places the component in the root layout file for site-wide tracking
- Automatically handles routing and performance metrics collection

### Verification

All validation steps passed:
- ✅ TypeScript compilation successful (`npm run typecheck`)
- ✅ Linter passed with no new errors (`npm run lint`)
- ✅ All tests passed (14/14 tests in the crypto test suite)

### Next Steps

To activate Speed Insights:
1. Deploy this change to Vercel
2. Enable Speed Insights in the Vercel dashboard (Project Settings → Speed Insights)
3. Monitor performance metrics as users visit the site

The SpeedInsights component will automatically track Core Web Vitals and send performance data to Vercel's analytics dashboard.
